-- =========================================================================
-- Dispatch — the REGISTRATION-SCOPE disposition (rights R3a).
--
-- ONE rule, in Fenel, consumed by BOTH mediated register paths: the sync ctx
-- native (`dispatch:register` / `dispatch:unregister` in
-- `fenel/modules/dispatch/ffi/dispatch-ffi.ts`) and the async IO handler
-- (`runtime/src/handlers/dispatch.ts`). The TypeScript on either side does
-- nothing but MARSHAL the frame's derived account in and mechanically DECODE
-- the answer; the decision is here.
--
-- Why it is a decision worth naming rather than an `if`:
--
--   * An account frame OWNS what it writes. The natives' `scope` ARGUMENT IS
--     IGNORED. A requested `global` is a NARROWING to the writer's account, not
--     an escalation; a requested tag is simply not honoured, because the tag
--     axis has no activators and nothing was ever visible under one.
--
--   * A frame with NO account — the registry bootstrap, the engine harness,
--     the kernel frame — MAY NOT WRITE. Global and tag instances are
--     boot-DECLARED, from `.fenel` sidecars. This is not a theoretical fence:
--     the design review EXECUTED it. An authentic account-A authority with an
--     EMPTY envelope was refused at `dispatch:register` directly and then wrote
--     a `{kind:"global"}` row anyway from inside a `SeWhere` predicate, because
--     the decider harness spreads its own cached bootstrap context and drops
--     the caller's authority. Under "a no-account frame keeps today's
--     behaviour" that write stays open; under this rule it refuses.
--
--   * There is no "foreign account" case to refuse. Ownership is DERIVED from
--     the authenticated authority, never argued, so a caller cannot name one.
--
-- rights R6: once delegation ships, the owning account may be the GRANT's
-- PARTITION rather than the caller's home account. That lands HERE — this
-- function is where the selection account is decided, and R6 must not inherit
-- "the mint account is always the visibility account".
-- =========================================================================

module dispatch where

-- The disposition's result. One case today; R6 adds the delegated form beside
-- it rather than widening `ScopeOwned`'s meaning.
@label "Registration scope"
@description "rights R3a — the scope a dispatch registration is written at. `ScopeOwned a` means the row is OWNED by account `a`: only a frame deriving `a` selects it, and only that frame deletes it. There is deliberately no global or tag case — those instances are boot-declared and unreachable from a native."
@tags "dispatch" "rights" "authority" "scope"
RegistrationScope = ScopeOwned accountId: String

@label "registrationScope"
@description "rights R3a — THE one rule both mediated register paths consume. Given the account DERIVED from the writing frame's authenticated authority, decide the scope its registration is written at. `Just a` owns the row; `Nothing` REFUSES, because global and tag instances are boot-declared and an authored predicate evaluated under the engine harness's bootstrap authority must not become a global write."
@tags "dispatch" "rights" "authority" "scope"
@category "engine-internal"
registrationScope : (frameAccount: Maybe String) -> Result String RegistrationScope
registrationScope frameAccount =
  case frameAccount of
    Just a ->
      if eq a "" then
        Err "dispatch registration requires a non-empty account frame"
      else
        Ok (ScopeOwned { accountId = a })
    _ ->
      Err "dispatch registration requires an account frame; global and tag instances are boot-declared"
